WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
(Episode 4)

3
00:01.040 --> 00:02.140
We have an emergency.

4
00:03.540 --> 00:06.020
Kataoka was taken.

5
00:06.880 --> 00:08.420
I'm afraid VOID is behind this.

6
00:11.550 --> 00:13.009
Did you sell him out?

7
00:13.010 --> 00:15.066
- What are you talking about? - I'm talking about Kataoka-san.

8
00:15.090 --> 00:16.090
What are you doing?

9
00:19.350 --> 00:21.270
- Odajima-san! - Let me go!

10
00:21.880 --> 00:23.080
- Hey! Get back here! - Stop!

11
00:23.540 --> 00:24.540
Hey!

12
00:27.220 --> 00:28.220
Stop right there!

13
00:40.740 --> 00:43.210
- Hey! - Don't move!

14
00:44.940 --> 00:45.940
Let me go!

15
00:50.540 --> 00:52.510
He really is a fascinating guy.

16
00:53.800 --> 00:57.220
Anyone who meets young Kataoka can't help falling for him.

17
00:59.040 --> 01:00.040
Yes.

18
01:05.300 --> 01:07.540
If anything goes south, contact Kumakura-san.

19
01:08.020 --> 01:09.020
Odajima-san.

20
01:25.680 --> 01:28.790
Since you want to see him so badly, I'll grant your wish.

21
01:35.380 --> 01:36.970
This is bad.

22
03:07.980 --> 03:09.580
Kataoka-san...

23
03:19.300 --> 03:20.300
In that instant,

24
03:22.030 --> 03:23.240
I knew.

25
03:25.440 --> 03:26.800
He was someone I must never touch.

26
03:31.220 --> 03:32.760
You get hopelessly drawn to him.

27
03:34.840 --> 03:36.600
Your eyes just follow him against your will.

28
03:38.360 --> 03:39.360
But I can't.

29
03:41.020 --> 03:42.020
I must not touch him.

30
03:50.400 --> 03:51.400
He is completely...

31
03:52.300 --> 03:53.300
out of reach.

32
04:20.640 --> 04:21.640
Boss...

33
04:23.340 --> 04:25.140
What good does it do if we're both captured?

34
04:42.840 --> 04:43.840
I'm sorry.

35
04:47.560 --> 04:48.660
To see you,

36
04:50.500 --> 04:51.600
this was the only way.

37
04:56.790 --> 05:00.020
Man, you really are something else.

38
06:13.300 --> 06:15.400
"The Journey To Killing You Season 2"

39
06:16.160 --> 06:17.160
Sorry.

40
06:17.460 --> 06:18.560
They got Odajima-san, too.

41
06:20.113 --> 06:23.299
Warehouse five in Awakuma City, right?

42
06:24.500 --> 06:25.500
Yes.

43
06:25.560 --> 06:27.660
Odajima-san is inside with VOID's guys.

44
06:28.400 --> 06:30.640
Kataoka-san is probably in there, too.

45
06:31.740 --> 06:32.740
Let's hope so.

46
06:34.060 --> 06:36.260
You weren't spotted tailing them, right?

47
06:36.920 --> 06:37.920
No, sir.

48
06:38.460 --> 06:40.460
I'll scope out the situation inside.

49
06:42.460 --> 06:44.060
Report back the second anything happens.

50
06:45.700 --> 06:46.700
Understood.

51
07:07.710 --> 07:08.800
Boss.

52
07:09.840 --> 07:12.010
I'm the one who called Kataoka and Odajima back.

53
07:12.540 --> 07:13.640
Please, let me go.

54
07:14.540 --> 07:17.280
They've already cut ties with the Kirii-gumi.

55
07:19.460 --> 07:21.740
Whether civilians live or die is none of our business.

56
07:21.860 --> 07:23.260
But why would ordinary civilians...

57
07:24.680 --> 07:26.180
get kidnapped in the first place?

58
07:27.140 --> 07:29.060
There has to be more to this.

59
07:50.010 --> 07:52.210
They think they're pulling the strings,

60
07:55.380 --> 07:57.140
when they're actually the ones being played.

61
08:09.610 --> 08:10.610
Excuse me.

62
08:12.060 --> 08:13.260
I'll take my leave now.

63
08:20.600 --> 08:22.200
The more clueless they are,

64
08:27.790 --> 08:29.590
the harder they dance to someone else's tune.

65
08:37.480 --> 08:38.480
Hey.

66
08:39.120 --> 08:40.480
That thing's filming us, isn't it?

67
08:43.860 --> 08:44.860
Yeah.

68
08:45.940 --> 08:47.220
Might as well give them a show.

69
08:51.180 --> 08:53.030
Recklessly chasing after me like that...

70
08:53.640 --> 08:55.360
Did you miss me that much?

71
08:57.620 --> 08:58.620
Hello?

72
09:00.450 --> 09:01.450
Hey!

73
09:05.180 --> 09:07.230
You're so easy to read.

74
09:10.220 --> 09:12.480
Hey, I'm starving over here!

75
09:12.880 --> 09:14.400
Bring us some food! Food!

76
09:15.880 --> 09:18.080
Or else we're really gonna start making out right here!

77
09:18.520 --> 09:20.970
If you don't wanna see that, bring us some grub!

78
09:23.000 --> 09:25.940
My grandpa went through hell after the war,

79
09:25.980 --> 09:28.540
so our family rule is to never skip three square meals a day!

80
09:29.240 --> 09:30.650
I know you're listening!

81
09:31.040 --> 09:32.280
Um, Boss...

82
09:32.880 --> 09:33.880
Huh?

83
09:56.680 --> 09:57.680
Whoa, hey.

84
09:57.900 --> 09:59.740
Are those brains of yours just for decoration?

85
10:00.220 --> 10:02.070
How are we supposed to eat tied up like this?

86
10:38.400 --> 10:39.500
Wait, what about me?

87
10:42.000 --> 10:43.800
How come only you get untied?

88
10:44.680 --> 10:45.700
Sorry about that...

89
10:46.850 --> 10:47.979
Oh, rice balls.

90
10:47.980 --> 10:49.180
How are you so calm right now?

91
10:50.120 --> 10:51.120
Sorry.

92
10:53.020 --> 10:55.560
Well, that makes one thing clear.

93
10:57.490 --> 10:59.880
If they're feeding us, they're not killing us right away.

94
11:01.340 --> 11:02.530
If they just wanted me dead,

95
11:04.620 --> 11:07.050
they would've just shot me back there.

96
11:09.580 --> 11:13.220
Going to the trouble of kidnapping me and keeping me alive means there's a reason.

97
11:14.320 --> 11:15.320
Right.

98
11:16.590 --> 11:17.980
Am I the target?

99
11:21.060 --> 11:23.030
Anyway, let's just eat first.

100
12:05.350 --> 12:06.570
Plum and tuna mayo.

101
12:06.640 --> 12:07.810
Which one do you want first?

102
12:07.840 --> 12:09.070
Tuna mayo, obviously.

103
12:10.310 --> 12:11.310
Okay.

104
12:25.820 --> 12:26.820
Here you go.

105
12:32.320 --> 12:33.320
Mmm...

106
12:35.420 --> 12:37.180
Come to think of it, we've done this before.

107
12:37.220 --> 12:39.020
You feeding me like this.

108
12:40.160 --> 12:41.160
Yes.

109
12:42.540 --> 12:46.190
Some kid asked me to help, so I spent all night keeping a baby bird warm.

110
12:48.500 --> 12:50.450
- I bought some food. - Oh.

111
12:54.770 --> 12:57.420
You idiot, how am I supposed to eat ramen?

112
12:57.560 --> 12:59.710
Didn't you just say my hands were occupied?

113
13:00.900 --> 13:01.900
I'm sorry.

114
13:03.110 --> 13:04.360
The rice balls will do.

115
13:04.600 --> 13:05.700
Hurry up and feed me.

116
13:10.560 --> 13:12.180
I got salmon and tuna mayo.

117
13:12.240 --> 13:13.720
Tuna mayo, obviously.

118
13:32.180 --> 13:33.180
That's right.

119
13:34.680 --> 13:37.000
You were so clumsy back then, you even spilled the ramen.

120
13:37.680 --> 13:38.880
You remember that really well.

121
13:39.110 --> 13:40.290
Of course I do.

122
13:43.440 --> 13:44.950
How could I ever forget?

123
13:52.100 --> 13:53.120
Here you go.

124
13:54.040 --> 13:55.040
Thanks.

125
14:00.670 --> 14:01.896
You've gotten pretty good at this.

126
14:01.920 --> 14:03.040
Your feeding skills, I mean.

127
14:03.500 --> 14:06.009
I can take care of you forever, Boss.

128
14:06.010 --> 14:07.220
Hey, what is this, elder care?

129
14:07.260 --> 14:08.500
I'm not that old yet.

130
14:09.050 --> 14:10.770
I'll take care of you when you're old, too.

131
14:11.820 --> 14:13.220
That almost sounds like a proposal.

132
14:15.600 --> 14:17.660
Does that mean you're gonna grow old with me?

133
14:21.580 --> 14:23.020
Though we're already married anyway.

134
14:28.020 --> 14:29.020
Hmm?

135
14:32.440 --> 14:33.440
Hmm?

136
14:37.370 --> 14:38.370
Hmm?

137
14:44.400 --> 14:45.500
I...

138
14:52.180 --> 14:53.570
have never once thought about...

139
14:56.020 --> 14:57.350
ever leaving your side.

140
15:05.690 --> 15:07.540
You're getting cuter by the day.

141
15:09.500 --> 15:10.530
Odajima.

142
15:30.300 --> 15:31.470
Um...

143
15:31.680 --> 15:32.720
Hmm?

144
15:34.000 --> 15:35.000
The reason you...

145
15:35.940 --> 15:37.220
married me in the first place...

146
15:41.920 --> 15:43.920
Now that you mention it, I still haven't told you.

147
15:44.620 --> 15:46.500
The reason I married you.

148
15:50.840 --> 15:53.000
I'll tell you once we get back.

149
15:54.070 --> 15:55.070
Ren.

150
16:05.000 --> 16:06.000
Odajima.

151
16:10.440 --> 16:11.510
No, not that.

152
16:13.840 --> 16:14.840
Kiss me.

153
16:17.940 --> 16:19.620
You make the first move for once.

154
16:21.780 --> 16:23.370
Give me a kiss and I'll tell you.

155
16:25.400 --> 16:26.400
Wait...

156
16:28.200 --> 16:29.200
Um...

157
16:33.530 --> 16:35.340
Seeing you look so reluctant...

158
16:35.910 --> 16:37.160
is so much fun.

159
16:40.160 --> 16:41.370
You haven't changed a bit.

160
16:42.790 --> 16:43.790
Come on.

161
16:50.500 --> 16:51.500
They're watching.

162
16:52.680 --> 16:53.680
Who cares?

163
16:54.340 --> 16:55.360
Let's give them a show.

164
16:56.260 --> 16:57.260
Come here.

165
17:20.490 --> 17:22.000
You will never...

166
17:22.330 --> 17:24.250
find happiness.

167
17:27.710 --> 17:29.270
Never...

168
17:29.420 --> 17:31.840
find happiness.

169
17:33.880 --> 17:34.880
Odajima...

170
17:39.380 --> 17:40.380
I...

171
17:42.520 --> 17:43.520
can never...

172
17:44.620 --> 17:45.620
be happy...

173
17:48.780 --> 17:49.780
I don't deserve...

174
17:51.220 --> 17:52.220
to be happy...

175
18:20.600 --> 18:21.760
Consider this a warning.

176
18:23.220 --> 18:24.740
Stay out of the Kirii-gumi's business.

177
18:25.866 --> 18:27.466
Do as you're told, and we'll let you go.

178
18:53.560 --> 18:56.320
Kataoka-san! Odajima-san!

179
19:00.950 --> 19:01.950
Boss...

180
19:02.260 --> 19:03.430
Please hurry...

181
19:04.560 --> 19:06.240
Who's behind this?

182
19:06.730 --> 19:07.779
Who's your boss?

183
19:07.780 --> 19:09.100
We don't take questions.

184
19:11.000 --> 19:12.870
You don't have a choice.

185
19:23.280 --> 19:24.480
Please save Kataoka...

186
19:25.780 --> 19:27.120
and Odajima.

187
19:27.790 --> 19:30.060
I told you, I have no obligation to step in.

188
19:30.340 --> 19:31.340
But...

189
19:31.880 --> 19:33.340
Kataoka did this for our family...

190
19:34.040 --> 19:35.880
I never asked him to.

191
19:38.340 --> 19:39.690
Calling the two of them back...

192
19:40.300 --> 19:41.640
was my mistake.

193
19:42.340 --> 19:43.340
Even so,

194
19:44.240 --> 19:47.320
you can't just leave them to die either, can you, Boss?

195
19:53.520 --> 19:56.020
You made this mess. Why should I clean it up?

196
19:58.960 --> 20:00.250
Our ties with those two...

197
20:01.240 --> 20:02.240
run deep.

198
20:04.740 --> 20:06.340
Letting ordinary civilians get killed...

199
20:07.620 --> 20:08.970
would bring shame to our family.

200
20:11.580 --> 20:12.580
Boss!

201
20:31.560 --> 20:32.560
Excuse me.

202
20:49.370 --> 20:51.050
Shut your mouth, go back to Okinawa,

203
20:51.780 --> 20:53.580
and stay out of Kirii-gumi's business, right?

204
20:56.520 --> 20:58.500
Not that I asked to get dragged into this.

205
21:06.510 --> 21:07.570
I refuse.

206
21:09.640 --> 21:11.950
I don't take orders from anyone.

207
21:14.920 --> 21:16.500
Is this about yakuza pride?

208
21:17.500 --> 21:20.140
Drop the tough guy act. You're out of the game.

209
21:20.320 --> 21:21.960
This has nothing to do with being yakuza.

210
21:22.440 --> 21:23.700
It's about my pride as a man.

211
21:25.640 --> 21:27.380
- Hey, Odajima. - Yes.

212
21:46.430 --> 21:47.820
What's going on?

213
21:48.160 --> 21:49.160
I'm sorry!

214
21:49.560 --> 21:50.716
We patted them down thoroughly...

215
21:50.740 --> 21:52.140
Come on, what are you, amateurs?

216
21:52.620 --> 21:54.990
Taking the shoes is Kidnapping 101.

217
21:57.700 --> 21:59.060
You're completely outnumbered.

218
22:00.180 --> 22:01.860
What's one little blade gonna do?

219
22:02.920 --> 22:04.440
You don't stand a chance.

220
22:06.760 --> 22:07.960
Fair point.

221
22:10.100 --> 22:11.200
However...

222
22:14.040 --> 22:15.810
it's plenty to kill just me.

223
22:17.880 --> 22:18.920
What are you doing?

224
22:19.400 --> 22:21.000
Take us to your boss.

225
22:21.820 --> 22:24.720
If you don't, he'll slit my throat.

226
22:26.090 --> 22:28.800
If we die, the Kirii-gumi will be out for blood.

227
22:29.600 --> 22:32.420
And your mastermind's grand plan goes up in smoke.

228
22:32.820 --> 22:34.740
Right after I kill you, I'll join you.

229
22:35.280 --> 22:36.280
Good.

230
22:36.480 --> 22:38.000
That's my wifey.

231
22:39.020 --> 22:41.000
Like you have the guts to do it!

232
22:42.500 --> 22:44.530
Never underestimate

233
22:44.720 --> 22:46.240
the resolve of an ex-yakuza!

234
22:57.870 --> 22:59.120
That's enough.

235
23:17.100 --> 23:17.960
(Next Episode Preview)

236
23:17.961 --> 23:20.260
The heads of the Koutokukai and Kirii-gumi.

237
23:20.560 --> 23:24.780
You said tensions are so high that an all-out war could break out if they meet, right?

238
23:24.900 --> 23:25.900
Damn it.

239
23:26.040 --> 23:30.360
They're no use to us alive, so let's just kill them.

240
23:30.540 --> 23:33.620
Come at me, you bastards!

241
23:34.370 --> 23:36.780
Looks like you guys are having a blast.

242
23:38.040 --> 23:39.040
Die!

243
23:40.670 --> 23:41.670
It's over.

244
23:44.170 --> 23:45.420
Kataoka-san!
